ot actually telling a complete story in  one go it does make it feel a little bit  odd because even by the metric of its  own series it feels weird the flow is  strange I'm not necessarily sure there  was a way around that if you accept the  decision to split this into two halves  but I feel like I would have been remiss  to not mention it I don't really have a  ton to say apart from just praising the  acting and especially the trio I mean  all the other actors are good as well no  one else  it's a highlight to the same degree oh I  really liked the animated segment  describing the deathly hallows and their  origin I really like the visual styling  the sort of puppetry sort of looking  marionette almost looking aspect to it I  quite enjoyed that I really liked that  visual presentation of it and yeah I  think it's a solid build-up to the to  the next one although I suspect when I  rank these at the end of this exercise  this is going to be more towards the  bottom because while it serves the  purpose it needs to which is to set us  up for a big blowout finish with the  with the eighth film actually taken as a  thing unto itself that there there's a  lot of stumbling points in it I still  enjoy it but yeah it's a bit of an  awkward beast this one Harry Potter and  the Deathly Hallows Part 1 you've seen  it what do you think about it whatever  your thoughts are drop something on the  comments let's talk about it there's a  bunch of stuff to do down there as well  you can like and subscribe that helps me  out quite a bit there's a patreon down  there if you want to help me keep this  thing going that helps me out even more  there's links other stuff besides click  on things they'll take your places  or don't you don't have to because at  the end of the day your council I'm just  running the meetings and until next time  this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

